WEBVTT

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.900
All done.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.610
See?

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.490
You did great, Hiyori.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.950
Sakura, you look adorable. Like a doll.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.910
I wouldn't—

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.490
Yes, you are.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.370
One look and Master will be dazzled for sure...

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.710
Not in a million years.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.340
Except for bread and cards,
he's not interested in anything, right?

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.430
Master must be in paradise right now.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.470
Welcome, Teruto.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.770
They're fresh out of the oven. Croissants.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:21.490
#08 Buried Memories

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.160
I never thought I'd see you again.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.160
Drop by for some bread sometime.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:28.500
Bread.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:37.340
MIKAZUKI STORE

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:34.960
When you were little,
you'd gobble up my bread just like this.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.550
Did I?

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.180
You always loved your bread and cards.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.590
That's all you would talk about with Kikka.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.800
What did you say about Kikka?

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:44.850
What?

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.730
Just that you two were always so close.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.900
Don't you remember playing at the shrine all the time?

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.940
Me and Kikka?

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:56.070
You used to love playing Build-Divide together.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.940
Is that right?

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:03.780
Don't you remember playing
while you waited for the bread to bake?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.410
Wait up, Brother!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:12.630
What's wrong?

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.170
Nothing.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:17.380
Azuma. Komugi. Don't stray too far.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.460
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.090
Sorry, I know my kids can be energetic.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.970
Actually, I want you to tell me more.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:26.560
Okay.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.020
I'm going to make the dough now, so sit tight.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.020
Teruto, I know you're in there.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.020
Kikka, the door is open.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:39.820
Teruto!

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:45.660
There you go again, Teruto,
going outside without telling Mom and Dad.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.450
They were really worried.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.750
What? You came here without asking?

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.790
I wanted some bread.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.670
I knew right away that Teruto had come here.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.250
Amazing, right?

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.590
You really love your brother, don't you?

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:00.880
Yeah!

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:06.260
Whenever Teruto wanders off,
I can find him no problem.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:11.680
I know. Today, why don't we try
kneading the dough together?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.390
Really?

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.890
I want to.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.520
Give it all you've got.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.490
Ai, we're done.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.160
Now we just wait for them to bake.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.410
What should we play while we wait?

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.120
Build-Divide.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.710
Kikka, have you memorized the rules?

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:42.720
Don't worry. I wanted to play with you,
so I tried really hard.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:49.760
I told you. Even if the unit takes damage,
it doesn't lose power.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.810
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:56.770
It's done.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.730
These are the ones Kikka made.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.030
These are Teruto's.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.650
Wow!

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:06.610
Weird. Why didn't mine puff up?

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.820
I guess you messed up a little?

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:12.750
Teruto is hopeless unless it has to do with cards.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:13.910
Here. Say ah—

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:14.620
Ah.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.080
Oh. Teruto!

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.330
Yum.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.550
Hey. Teruto, you dummy.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:26.800
This is a photo from back then.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.890
This is us?

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.560
You two were so close.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:36.640
Due to your parents' circumstances,
you two had to be separated.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:41.940
When Kikka found out,
she took it so hard, she started bawling.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.070
This memory.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.540
I'm so glad I got to see you today.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.160
Yeah. Thanks to you, I can see my path.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.420
Get home safe, okay?

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.710
- Mom.
- Mom.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.170
The croissants. They were good.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.260
I'll visit again.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.890
Right. See you later.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.690
<i>You two were always so close.</i>

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.650
<i>Don't you remember playing at the shrine all the time?</i>

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:27.650
I know that I hate Kikka.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.870
That's...

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.580
This is where Kikka and I used to play.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.390
What's going on?

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.810
So you finally showed up.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:56.930
You're...

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:01.020
The you who remembers his past,
or the you who doesn't remember his past.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.310
Which of you will end up being more intriguing?

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:04.900
What are you talking about?

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.440
I'd rather see the more intriguing you.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.280
Abracadabra.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.070
Bam!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.540
You're...

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.910
Kikka?

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.540
Hey. What the hell is going on?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.210
I'm bored, you see.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.170
Higuma is taking so long to show me my dream.

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:31.680
So I'm taking it on myself to move things along.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:37.060
You realize how unreliable your memory is, right?

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.810
Now that you mention it, this is my room.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:46.110
This is a good time to remember. The real you.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.450
Wait. Is this me?

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.620
How cute!

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.250
I was in a Rebuild Battle with the King.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:02.040
With Sakura, Hiyori, and Naomitsu.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.670
Now then. You go and have some fun.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.000
Someone was just here.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.260
Teruto, what's the matter?

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.590
Rebuild Battle...

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.180
Rebuild. What's that?

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:18.510
Huh? What was it again?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.520
Anyway, let's play Build-Divide.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:24.400
Sure. I'll be happy to defeat you every time.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.110
Bring it on, Kikka.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.820
I'll beat you this time for sure.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.860
This one. Right?

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:38.120
Huh? What do I do next?

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:42.290
Don't show me your hand in the middle of a battle.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:46.460
So you put the only Ace in your hand with your Energy?

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:49.670
I wanted to use this color Energy.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.550
I'll take you down with this.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:01.850
This Command can take down lots of units,
so using it now would be a waste.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.100
What? Come on.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:11.940
That's right. I taught her how to play,
and in the end I'd win.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:17.160
You'd better learn how to battle now,
or you'll have a hard time when you grow up.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.870
When I grow up,
I'll be too powerful to ever lose to you.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.290
In your dreams.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.120
Using Bloom to attack.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.250
You sure love Bloom, huh?

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:30.420
Huh?

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:32.340
Yeah, she's strong.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.590
You've never beaten her, have you?

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:37.300
Got it.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.760
Iora. Go!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.390
Territory. Build Arise.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.480
Heavy Artillery Base Vulbabylon.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:56.820
I...

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:58.910
Iora?

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.700
I thought Kikka's Ace was Margreia.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.790
What's wrong? Hurry, let's play.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.540
What is this?

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.170
I see.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.630
I'll draw three cards.

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:15.130
I just got a great idea.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.590
I'll put this one back on top.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.390
When I use Iora to attack Bloom...

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:23.430
I'll use this ability for this Command Card.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.310
Now I'll use Vulbabylon's ability to copy.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.690
This will give Iora 13,500 power.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:34.860
See? Even if Bloom uses her ability now,
you can't beat me, can you?

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.990
Iora. Do it!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.120
Bloom!

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.750
Okay. Bloom loses.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:54.210
I'm thrilled. I beat Bloom for the first time.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:11:00.930
Hey. It's your turn now.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.100
Demonic Armor.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.730
Two-Hit Attack.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:13.150
Okay, my turn.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.480
Difference in lives, two to four.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:19.700
I totally remember everything you taught me.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:22.360
Command. Blue Burst.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.160
Using Vulbabylon to copy.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.990
Inflicting all units with ten thousand damage.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.460
Everyone, out of my sight!

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.920
Now I'm using Iora to attack Teruto.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.590
Drawing two cards with New Weapon Development.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.050
Go!

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:52.190
Shot Trigger. Cursed Trump Card.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.150
Destroying Iora.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.610
Hey, Teruto. Can I use this one now?

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.780
Quick...

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:03.820
Collapse of Rationality.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.530
I'm eliminating your trump card.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:09.830
Yay, I did it!

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:13.170
Zero lives left. My turn.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.630
Activating Casino of Fate's ability.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.840
Buster Cards. Zero.

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:20.670
Destroying Iora.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.090
Iora.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:25.930
Next, Command. Evil Deal.

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:28.260
Moving two cards from the Cemetery to my hand.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:31.480
Partial Dealer. Accept.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:32.730
End of turn.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.020
I was so close.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.940
You're just going to block me, so I can't end you.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:40.400
Just kidding.

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:41.860
Accept.

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:46.620
Frida?

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:49.830
You can't block this one. Right?

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.040
Yeah.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:00.800
Just do it.

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.930
I did it. I...

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:12.140
That's right. This battle...

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:16.400
For the first time, I beat Teruto.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.820
I lost...

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.480
...to Kikka?

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.360
Teruto. What did you think of that battle?

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:27.070
Wasn't it fun?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:28.450
Let's play again.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:29.990
That was a fluke.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.040
It had to be.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.380
That's right. I lost to Kikka.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:44.300
Presented by Ishinome Film Revivals.
"The First Day I Lost to My Little Sister."

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.340
Did you enjoy the show?

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.050
Now, take a look at this.

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:57.270
This is the story of a little girl who wanted
to have fun and play with her big brother.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.400
The second act is about to start.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:02.780
This is game over.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.150
Using Frida to attack Teruto.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.700
Using Iora to attack Teruto.

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:09.740
Attacking Teruto.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:11.200
Attacking Teruto.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:12.910
Attacking Teruto.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.750
What's going on?

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.160
I just keep losing.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.160
I...

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.840
This is fun. It's so fun beating you, Teruto.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.170
Probably because you're so good, right?

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.510
Let's play again.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:28.840
Not playing.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.140
Huh? Why not?

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:34.890
I don't want to.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:43.320
That's right. I was losing to Kikka
more and more. That's why...

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.690
Wait. Come back, Teruto.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.110
Why? How come?

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:51.070
I practiced so hard.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:54.740
You're the one that taught me about Build-Divide.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:15:00.290
Since that day, the little sister kept begging
her big brother, her voice shaking.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:04.090
Every day and night, over and over.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.630
It was you who made me a strong player.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.840
Because you said I wasn't fun since I was weak.

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:18.520
That's why I worked so hard to be a good player,
so you would enjoy playing with me.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:26.480
Hey, play with me. Play with me, Teruto.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:30.450
Look at me, will you?

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:38.080
Look at me. Teruto.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:42.670
What can I do for you to play with me again?

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.290
Teruto.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:51.970
Listen, Teruto.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:58.180
Kikka...

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:00.730
Play with me.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:06.520
Then one day, the two are forced to part
due to their parents' circumstances.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:13.200
Tomorrow, we have to say goodbye, right?

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:19.330
Will we never see each other again?

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.870
I wonder how far your house is?

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.790
Very far.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.720
You talked to me.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.220
Listen, Teruto. I don't want you to go.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.050
I want to be with you.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.680
I don't want us to be apart.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.270
I want to play with you more.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.100
I want to play Build-Divide with you.

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:47.400
I...

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.660
Well, you hate me now, right?

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.910
That's why you won't play with me?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:04.290
But just one more time.
I want to play with you one more time.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.000
Just one more will do.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.210
I'm meeting up with my friends tomorrow.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.010
It can be after that.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:13.920
It will be dark.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:16.510
I don't care. I'll be fine.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:20.890
Please, one last time.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:25.230
One more time, then.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:30.730
Okay. Let's meet at the shrine like we always do.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:32.150
See you tomorrow.

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.990
Then, on that last day...

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.700
Gone. It's gone.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:46.040
My deck. But why? I know I put it here.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:50.130
What should I do? It's almost time.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:51.590
What should I do?

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:59.640
Teruto. Teruto!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.520
He's not here? Teruto...

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.270
Teru—

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:11.110
I'm sorry. I lost my deck.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.230
That's why I got here late.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:17.490
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:23.450
Teruto, just one more time.
One more time would have been enough.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.910
Teruto.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:29.960
See you.

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:36.420
That's how this sad story of two siblings ends.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:41.510
The little sister, separated from her brother,
became the most powerful.

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:44.470
Eventually becoming the King.

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:47.270
Let me out of here.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:52.400
Now that you remember everything,
what do you plan to do now?

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.730
Please.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:03.240
Your hatred for the King is what's stirring you, right?

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.700
It was nothing but a path of lies.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.750
But are you still going to battle your little sister?

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.250
I don't know.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.540
Then hurry and make up your mind.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:48.910
That day, I hid and buried Kikka's deck.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:58.800
It's all my fault. All of it.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.680
<i>By the way, Teruto.</i>

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:07.390
<i>Why is Kikka the King now?</i>

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:12.850
<i>Kikka once said to me,
"I wonder if Teruto is where the King is at?"</i>

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.190
<i>She was searching for a way to get there.</i>

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:18.440
<i>But along the way, she became the King herself.</i>

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:21.240
Rebuild.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:25.120
I was familiar with this battle.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:29.870
I...

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.420
Master!

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.210
Welcome home.

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:41.220
Sakura? Hiyori?

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:45.090
We thought you'd be home by now,
so we stopped by to check on you.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:46.300
Were you fine getting there?

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.260
Good for you for getting home safely.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.100
Good for me?

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.480
Hey, you're empty-handed?

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.310
You went to the bakery, right?

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:55.900
We were looking forward to you
bringing something back for us.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:57.360
I forgot.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.320
But I do have these.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:01.530
Key chips. Three of them.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:03.650
You battled all on your own?

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:05.450
Something wrong with that?

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:08.700
What is it?

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:12.750
Master, you're up on your own two feet.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:14.330
My, how you've grown.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:15.250
Well, excuse me.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.380
I'm going to go buy some bread.

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:18.790
Aren't you full already?

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:21.630
Master, you can't go by yourself.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:24.010
Don't worry, I'll go with him.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:26.510
Sakura, I'll be fine.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:29.890
Not happening. You always get lost.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:33.310
You can't go by yourself.

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:36.520
You always get lost, Teruto.

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:39.520
Teruto?

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.150
You're right.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:44.450
I want you to come with me.

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:54.330
Kikka.

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:59.170
Hey. You seem motivated all of a sudden.
What happened?

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:01.960
I found the exit is all.

00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:06.340
If we get two more, we can see the King, right?

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:09.640
Yes. I know you'll get them in no time.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.220
I'm sure.

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:14.480
Do you really hate the King that much?

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:19.770
It's strange that your little sister
is the one you want to take down.

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:21.690
Maybe the truth is, you really—

00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:24.110
No. There's no question.

00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:26.200
She's my little sister.

00:22:31.530 --> 00:22:34.540
Teruto? What's wrong? Teruto.

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:39.960
I'm so hungry.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:46.800
Seriously. You're a handful.

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:55.520
That's it. You'll reach these heights
by battling the King whom you hate.

00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:58.440
Following the script I wrote.

00:22:59.690 --> 00:23:03.770
When the battle between you two starts...

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:05.360
At that very moment...

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:08.570
Teruto.

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:16.200
Lord Higuma. Kikka is running out of time.

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:18.120
Indeed.

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:21.920
Just get here already, Teruto Kurabe.

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:29.970
TO BE CONTINUED

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:32.300
Only one chip left.

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:36.520
Until I reach the King, I can't afford to lose.

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:39.480
Come, let's go. To our ending.

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:39.980
#09 Reach for the Stars
